[{"id":"VRCE-1-54-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words of his, Surabhi created (an army). And, O king, Pahlavas by hundreds brought into being by her lowing, begin even in Viśvāmitra's sight to commit havoc upon his forces. Thereat, exceedingly angered, with eyes expanded in ire, that king commenced to slay the Pahlavas with various weapons. And beholding the Pahlavas by hundreds afflicted by Viśvāmitra, she again created grim-visaged Sakas mixed with Yavanas. And the field became thronged with the Sakas mixed with Yavanas, of dazzling splendour, exceedingly fierce, resembling golden filaments, bearing sharp scimitars and adzes, and clad in yellow apparel. And that entire host (of Viśvāmitra) was being consumed by them like to flaming fires. Then the exceedingly powerful Viśvāmitra hurled weapons at them; and with these the Yavanas, Kambojas and Barbaras (Barbarians) became sore afflicted.' Then the exceedingly powerful Viśvāmitra hurled weapons at them; and with these the Yavanas, Kambojas and Barbaras (Barbarians) became sore afflicted.' And beholding them sore harassed, and overwhelmed by Visvāmitra's weapons, Vasistha directed (Sabala) saying, 'o cow of plenty, do you create (fresh troops), through your Yoga power.'","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-54-17","DUTT-1-55-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"676ba96a036aaa870ae1de03a8ba7c9671e35af037ec973a45d8107cf2057b33","compact":"aec38d190766d4c67de0712c654006f64d7d97e4cb8e4f19c37f6da1fbc72e5e","nasal":"43751b4255fe9923ccd9c8f39621e928707f42e564578ed1092fef119156b986"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":2,"english":"And from her roar, there came into being Kamvojas, resembling the Sun. And from her udders sprang Barbaras, arms in hand; and from her mysterious parts, Yavanas; from her anus, Sakas; and from the pores of her skin, those barbarians, Hārītas and Kirātas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.379,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1836da0b7478b092afe0fc0c8378bdd2c1aea332629e0791046b5500ce759e04","compact":"014270fd26aa534626087e651f073fae8463b7a0c84114beda8bd2d6379b5727","nasal":"a2d637fafa177d0a9407789857c2d8b1db4f6c82d4d8bb476752e77dfc6dd3d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":3,"english":"And from her roar, there came into being Kamvojas, resembling the Sun. And from her udders sprang Barbaras, arms in hand; and from her mysterious parts, Yavanas; from her anus, Sakas; and from the pores of her skin, those barbarians, Hārītas and Kirātas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.45,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d120dcd6d2a97c227d048dfcd6b7d56d4cbaa9420f7fe7693a754b9b667d5bc9","compact":"02e9291ead28e78f64140998d395d1d25d6aa9bdcc888fa3339885685f58ff50","nasal":"02e9291ead28e78f64140998d395d1d25d6aa9bdcc888fa3339885685f58ff50"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":4,"english":"And, (descendant of Raghu, Viśvāmitra's entire host consisting of foot, and elephant, and horse, and car, was exterminated by them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.734,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33a0e7ea374b222852495397a51094eb9e46d30ac264aeec7e631e0778778b61","compact":"0a8a791420ba4d3d8e0fcd06e4070ac1831c4bb99b50b534229b16f24b65a352","nasal":"fbd563093d27e27ae131af1a44c920584d02b1c4a1449861e2a9e349d47aed5b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":5,"english":"Seeing the army annihilated by the highsouled Vasiştha, the hundred sons of Viśvāmitra, equipped with various weapons, rushed in high ire against that best of mantra-reciting ones. Thereupon, uttering a roar, that mighty ascetic consumed them quite. In a moment, Viśvāmitra's sons together with horse and car and foot were reduced to ashes by the high-souled Vasistha.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-4","DUTT-1-55-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ea34c6bbd6636a7ac987ac6678e5f0b0fd2eb719edc497c6227ae00cd53ef74","compact":"fc4ae50c6abc4ed157ea5a67f573fded2bb806c65b560eb34b9867c74e8b7bc8","nasal":"fc4ae50c6abc4ed157ea5a67f573fded2bb806c65b560eb34b9867c74e8b7bc8"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":6,"english":"Seeing the army annihilated by the highsouled Vasiştha, the hundred sons of Viśvāmitra, equipped with various weapons, rushed in high ire against that best of mantra-reciting ones. Thereupon, uttering a roar, that mighty ascetic consumed them quite.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b7e7d0c75b22ac34d1f9521f2c8172e25df440f53062ed30409c19ffe0a18b45","compact":"b657aba9e4d67ea7d0a8192e74bf15cc9655f3c26ca0ca03389e51c6f23dcc79","nasal":"3423790bb60a460e21a2ce20b9cb73424a9e279f21370e5b6cda260703964946"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":7,"english":"Seeing the army annihilated by the highsouled Vasiştha, the hundred sons of Viśvāmitra, equipped with various weapons, rushed in high ire against that best of mantra-reciting ones. Thereupon, uttering a roar, that mighty ascetic consumed them quite. In a moment, Viśvāmitra's sons together with horse and car and foot were reduced to ashes by the high-souled Vasistha.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-4","DUTT-1-55-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee274bb17b1211ef4f5b9302632a94f55beb7e8994058ac6d654368d01281f01","compact":"3dc2c9e32dd93e31dade4b3467e29836d0f39775c2c50bbd4ee8cecf4b8fa5bb","nasal":"3dc2c9e32dd93e31dade4b3467e29836d0f39775c2c50bbd4ee8cecf4b8fa5bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":8,"english":"And witnessing them all destroyed, together with the army, the illustrious Viśvāmitra, covered with shame, became plunged in thought.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba6d77d0e386999c2168c74708382a5536c9fad13ed88d83f6fd4a5285b23299","compact":"572940b425c792a46e45a934b62e40dfe074e1cc44f9660f4d1cfab0acf38997","nasal":"b0f44f8cf030f2191082a339f7e63babd78ef80465da07fcbd2a7dc34a19f0c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":9,"english":"And like to a tideless ocean or a fangless snake, he instantly became shorn of his effulgence, like to the sun overwhelmed by Rahu.* *A Daitya with the tail of a dragon, whose head was served from his body by Vişnu; but being immortal, the head and tail retained their separate existence, and being transferred to the stellar sphere, became the author of eclipses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.644,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"93f7360f30f94500c66d5ebfd0f74a2dea79f2d83dc1a9ce9a2849278d1a984a","compact":"705c6c64cad387e5f201e81206faf5d9a912558234374c76d27d47dfa12c29af","nasal":"705c6c64cad387e5f201e81206faf5d9a912558234374c76d27d47dfa12c29af"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":10,"english":"And deprived of his forces and sons, he appeared like a bird bereft of its wings; and losing his entire army and with it the high spirits that it had inspired him with, his heart died within him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.736,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"665f762dea0da1a44bd3026f7d42580f54439495a4c7b9b3a7818ead85a134f3","compact":"ad7712d39c23494f9fc325f9419ed60b2952566bfe72a1e0509a27f85cf0856a","nasal":"ad7712d39c23494f9fc325f9419ed60b2952566bfe72a1e0509a27f85cf0856a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":11,"english":"Then entrusting one of his (remaining) sons with the sovereignty, with, 'Do you rule the earth agree ably to the duties of the Kșatriya,' he went into the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0babfcbb9aca1a089daba12b927504e22aa5f3ebce9f0052c57ad855093b5e89","compact":"4c2251f6266b115e993f005f28c2bd08e34fc8d8dad97d07f4fb350d9ba0e1a6","nasal":"4c2251f6266b115e993f005f28c2bd08e34fc8d8dad97d07f4fb350d9ba0e1a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":12,"english":"And repairing to the side of the Himavat inhabited by Kinnaras and Serpents that one of mighty asceticism began to perform austerities with the view of propitiating Mahādeva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8daeb073acc3ce5c56bbd2d49277579ec26f1512517a3a58937860d023b6fd2a","compact":"c8abd3c18decae189f5c957b6a17fb784a8d4424b6d59a96a04abee7652fee3e","nasal":"a23f4521a22a397f31b1d024328699d237f7cdf43029a0bdc4324bf28595159d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":13,"english":"On a certain occasion the lord of the celestials, Vrsadhvaja,* intending to confer a boon, appeared before a mighty ascetic Viśvāmitra. *An appellation of Śiva: meaning who has the bull for his vehicle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24e8cfe76dfc287f639a857b648dd0be50d9facf4d83b7a94b3254ea7fa74030","compact":"8350084bddf16d7a20da25660e10d283738b1ab4bcaa0e0fa4c35943e8809c11","nasal":"8350084bddf16d7a20da25660e10d283738b1ab4bcaa0e0fa4c35943e8809c11"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":14,"english":"What for, O king, art you performing penance?. Do you unfold what you have to say. I am for conferring a boon: do you express what boon you would obtain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"61fe695b4a2b71a11976c1629c09de6e351b07a4db51248aacd718a437756141","compact":"c229e0b091763e158978a6cf31628a9efe291d0f76640ea8690ac4932bc0f381","nasal":"6c216166dca337abbad4fdee2df380798dd99e837d0f3f82f36e6ae35334a78a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":15,"english":"Thus addressed by that god, that performer of mighty austerities, Viśvāmitra, bowing down to him, addressed him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"381aaaabc782db3168a24168afb7bc4195c0f3aecbf582700acfaf6f9e4cb8a3","compact":"e9a856075cd6fbc1c8870419f51f9a4ae6c372c8fdeb5c0bbe0c9dd7132f14f5","nasal":"e9a856075cd6fbc1c8870419f51f9a4ae6c372c8fdeb5c0bbe0c9dd7132f14f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":16,"english":"If, O mighty god, you are pleased (with me), do you confer upon me the science of archery with all its mysteries and mantras, as well as its virtues of helping from far and near.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5bc854b436fe06650e2e83318aeec886641a2790eeaa8db1e3537cabaf6245ac","compact":"c1f085e01b20b45d72ec7cf937111f1750e7e07fdee2befaf83d03c5a3199341","nasal":"afd567833ea02e9f70d3a6ca11c4eae3abfeca8af00b4a3acd6136095c70db04"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":17,"english":"O sinless one, may all those weapons that are with the celestials and the Dānavas and the Maharșis and the Gandharvas and the Yakşas and the Rākşasa, shine on me ! May this my desire be granted me through your grace, O god of gods!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7838ff661d82c143813739a6298f2be60406d72ce107f234875cb9e78255513b","compact":"1c55f2df232beb96aaab6caec9012a8492d00497976ec6433df6683ba8bb4e08","nasal":"1258eb3365c10f1c38198aa3a3170e8ff2f0d0c506b2c4c995e3ba9bff6400ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":18,"english":"Thereupon, saying, 'Be it so' the lord of the celestials vanished. And obtaining the arms from the lord of the celestials, the mighty Viśvāmitra, naturally haughty, became swelled with insolence.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a6f66bae7ef82731e58e4fafe54fd68d32c02b38e2a4f5d7b50c206e41c3b38","compact":"9fad5a2f02a8103e5896de380ff6635475b755fa86a021bd1f38de86ea67ebcb","nasal":"9fad5a2f02a8103e5896de380ff6635475b755fa86a021bd1f38de86ea67ebcb"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":19,"english":"Thereupon, saying, 'Be it so' the lord of the celestials vanished. And obtaining the arms from the lord of the celestials, the mighty Viśvāmitra, naturally haughty, became swelled with insolence.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.671,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdb9e52f4524af9dba442a18a650b409936699b565d207c907502c8a7309db13","compact":"ad03623435f3e91fdd6623abaa47a033363a67e08419769d553f7227765e3028","nasal":"ad03623435f3e91fdd6623abaa47a033363a67e08419769d553f7227765e3028"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":20,"english":"Surcharged with energy, like to the sea during the equinox, he considered, O Rāma, as if that foremost of saints, Vasistha, was already slain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.679,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ad761b401cc242d0a2676994673c2549952fa9b3f4de770d150e6396d2303b5","compact":"678eb316d0dfd2e9629b4b72655c0ecef35061dd38b2de4105f70a9c49786c2f","nasal":"678eb316d0dfd2e9629b4b72655c0ecef35061dd38b2de4105f70a9c49786c2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":21,"english":"And repairing to Vasistha's asylum, the king began to discharge weapons; and by their energy the hermitage began to burn.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.826,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5ca308808c286a1a32b8b42b354cfe57d6ece4418ddd4b13012f5a493270340","compact":"6969c0d7bd5e6242d16f4a93faed95e8a2529cd0d5548b270e10d7f3ed5bb5ad","nasal":"6969c0d7bd5e6242d16f4a93faed95e8a2529cd0d5548b270e10d7f3ed5bb5ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-54-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":54,"verse":22,"english":"Beholding those weapons discharged by the intelligent Viśvāmitra, the ascetics, overtaken by fear, by hundreds began to fly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.866,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-55-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1054022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0625d4153fc3ad5665f68063691e268a2525f44143fe06eb9cfb596f42278c3e","compact":"7369e504eadf372c05332ec951a46addbe828c5701a36c38fc66c17d